t getting value from a bet. I should realize equity by checking this time and hoping they check back.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: Currently, I hold Two Pair (Tens and Sevens) with an Ace kicker, formed by my 10 and the board's 10, 7, 7, A. The opponent has checked on every street (Pre-flop, Flop, Turn, and River), indicating a likely weak hand or missed draws, though a trap with a 7 or slow-played Ace is possible. Betting here yields thin value; worse hands (like a pair of 6s or lower pocket pairs) will likely fold, while better hands (any Ace or Trip 7s) will call or raise. Checking guarantees a showdown where I likely have the best hand or chop with another 10, avoiding the risk of a check-raise.\n\nReason: My hand has significant showdown value but is not strong enough to confidently bet for value on the river given the Ace on the board. The opponent's passivity suggests I am likely ahead, and checking eliminates the risk of losing more chips to a trap while securing the pot if I am ahead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
